  "report": "Long question rows now show both yes/no buttons, and short rows look the same as before.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/components/QuestionRow.tsx`, the question `Text` had no shrink behaviour inside the horizontal row. A long title took the full row width and pushed the yes/no pills off-screen.\n\n**Change** (one line, `QuestionRow.tsx`, `styles.question`):\n```diff\n-  question: { fontSize: 15 },\n+  question: { flexShrink: 1, fontSize: 15 },\n```\nThe title now wraps and the pills keep their size.\n\n**What I checked on the iPhone 17 simulator, with Metro reloading the change:**\n- **Before the fix:** the long Cleaning rows had no yes/no buttons. These were the toilets question and \"Is the area behind the bakery ovens…\".\n- **After the fix, long rows:**\n  - Both rows wrap their text over several lines and show both buttons, fully on-screen at the right edge.\n  - The accessibility tree lists a yes and a no button for each, with frames inside the screen.\n  - The high-risk \"!\" marker still sits on the left.\n- **After the fix, short rows** (\"Bins emptied\", \"Trolley bay tidy\", \"Entrance mats clean\", the Shelves rows): they sit in the same positions as in my before-fix capture, with the pills right after the title.\n- **Tap test:** I tapped \"yes\" on the bakery row. The pill highlighted and the header went from \"0 of 48\" to \"1 of 48 answered\". That answer is only in the running app's memory and disappears when the app restarts.\n\nI only checked the Safety, Food safety, Cleaning and Shelves sections. I didn't scroll through the rest of the 48 questions or test large Dynamic Type sizes."
}